  "novel_mechanics_found": "L4 has three movable multicolor pieces controlled by seven handles (2/3/2), not six; each piece must touch its uniquely color-matched dotted socket, while five additional unmatched dotted glyphs are real landing blockers/decoys. L5 introduces two black carrier pieces controlled by two and three purple-centered handles. A carrier picks up a partially colored black cargo when it overlaps it; the payload then moves with the carrier. Complementary solid halves must be fused first (orange+maroon and cyan+tan), after which the fused payload is delivered to the matching two-color dotted template. Delivering the orange/maroon pair visibly consumed six dots of each color. L5 retained a hard 60-click meter.",
  "narrative": "Resolved and replayed the 82-action verified prefix to level 3, then solved L4 live on a clean 59-click attempt. The fresh-reset reproduction gate replayed the resulting 141-action sequence and reached level 4 with reproduced=true. Continued through three L5 explorations: discovered carrier pickup, complementary-cargo fusion, and successfully delivered the orange/maroon pair; also fused the cyan/tan pair and routed it toward the upper-right template. The final optimized L5 attempt exhausted the 60-click meter during that last upward delivery, so no L5 win was observed and the verified frontier remains level 4.",
  "gotchas": [
    "L4's three pieces use seven handles: the handle-count split is 2/3/2. The prior six-handle preview missed one.",
    "The L4 board contains five unmatched dotted glyphs in addition to the three true color-matched sockets; their cells block handle landings even though they are decoys for the win condition.",
    "Clicking any rendered cell inside another handle's diamond can silently switch selection instead of moving the current handle. Several geometrically valid-looking routes fail this way.",
    "A handle may become partly hidden underneath its own carrier/cargo. Clicking an exposed outer diamond cell can still select it, but clicking the occluded center is unreliable.",
    "On L4/L5 the effective click meter is 60 actions: rejected clicks and selection clicks consume it, and the next action after depletion produces GAME_OVER.",
    "L5 requires a three-stage interaction: overlap a solid half to pick it up, overlap its complementary solid half to fuse them, then move the fused two-color payload onto the matching dotted template.",
    "For L5, orange+maroon maps to the lower-left orange/maroon dotted template; cyan+tan maps to the upper-right cyan/tan dotted template. The other dotted glyphs are blockers/decoys.",
    "GameAction.RESET cleanly restores the current level while preserving levels_completed; failed exploratory actions and RESETs must be omitted when constructing the clean reproduction sequence."
  ],
